If a native mobile app is already available, inspect its notification architecture.

If the application is currently a web app or PWA, support the appropriate web push capabilities.

For native mobile push, use an appropriate provider such as Firebase Cloud Messaging or Apple Push Notification service, depending on the existing app architecture.

Do not pretend that a website notification automatically becomes a native app push notification.

Use one notification backend and user identity system so notifications can be delivered across supported devices.

### E. Offline notification delivery

If a seller is offline when a buyer sends a message:
- Save the message in the database.
- Create a persistent notification.
- Queue delivery where supported.
